{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "day": 3,
  "level": 1,
  "title": { "en": "Easy consonants and silent h", "es": "Consonantes fáciles y la hache muda" },
  "objectives": [
    "Say p, t and k without a puff of air",
    "Never pronounce h",
    "Hear the soft d between vowels",
    "Say please and excuse me"
  ],
  "teach": [
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "Good news: **m, n, f, l** and **s** sound much as they do in English.\n\n**p, t** and **k** are softer. English puts a puff of air after them (hold your hand in front of your mouth and say *top*). Spanish doesn't, so **todo** and **papá** barely move the air."
    },
    { "kind": "sound", "grapheme": "h", "ipa": "∅", "tip": "Always silent. Just start on the vowel: hola = OH-la, hotel = o-TEL.", "examples": ["hola", "hotel", "hoy", "ahora"] },
    { "kind": "sound", "grapheme": "t", "ipa": "t̪", "tip": "The tongue tip touches the back of your top teeth, not the ridge behind them. No puff of air.", "examples": ["todo", "tomate", "hotel"] },
    { "kind": "sound", "grapheme": "c · qu", "ipa": "k", "tip": "c before a, o, u, and qu before e, i, both sound like k. The u in que/qui is silent.", "examples": ["casa", "queso", "aquí"] },
    {
      "kind": "sound",
      "grapheme": "d (soft)",
      "ipa": "ð",
      "tip": "Between vowels, after r and at the end of a word, d softens to the 'th' in 'this': just a light touch of the tongue on the teeth. After a pause, n or l it's a firm d.",
      "examples": ["nada", "todo", "Madrid", "perdón"]
    },
    { "kind": "note", "md": "You'll hear the soft d everywhere in Spain: **nada** ≈ NA-tha, **Madrid** ≈ ma-DRITH. Keep it gentle. It's a light touch, not a strong English *th*." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Por favor.", "en": "Please.", "note": "Tap the r's lightly, like the tt in American 'butter'. The v sounds like b." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Perdón.", "en": "Sorry. / Excuse me.", "note": "Use it when you bump into someone, need to get past, or want someone's attention. Stress -DÓN." }
  ],
  "vocab": [
    { "id": "por-favor", "es": "por favor", "en": "please", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "poɾ faˈβoɾ", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "perdon", "es": "perdón", "en": "sorry, excuse me", "pos": "interj", "ipa": "peɾˈðon", "note": "Also: perdona (to someone you'd call tú).", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "hoy", "es": "hoy", "en": "today", "pos": "adv", "ipa": "ˈoi" },
    { "id": "ahora", "es": "ahora", "en": "now", "pos": "adv", "ipa": "aˈoɾa" },
    { "id": "aqui", "es": "aquí", "en": "here", "pos": "adv", "ipa": "aˈki" },
    { "id": "nada", "es": "nada", "en": "nothing", "pos": "pron", "ipa": "ˈnaða" },
    { "id": "todo", "es": "todo", "en": "everything, all", "pos": "pron", "ipa": "ˈtoðo" },
    { "id": "hotel", "es": "el hotel", "en": "the hotel", "pos": "noun", "gender": "m", "ipa": "oˈtel" },
    { "id": "queso", "es": "el queso", "en": "the cheese", "pos": "noun", "gender": "m", "ipa": "ˈkeso" },
    { "id": "ordenador", "es": "el ordenador", "en": "the computer", "pos": "noun", "gender": "m", "ipa": "oɾðenaˈðoɾ", "note": "Latin America: la computadora." }
  ],
  "exercises": [
